What is a Contaminated Trial?
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Definition:

\series default
 In clinical research,
 contamination refers to situations where control group participants receive the intervention or intervention group participants fail to follow the protocol.
 
\begin_inset Argument 1
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

1-
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Impact:

\series default
 This blurs the distinction between groups,
 making it harder to detect whether the intervention truly works.
\begin_inset Argument item:2
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

2-
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Example:

\series default
 In a trial testing a new health program,
 if control participants independently adopt parts of the program,
 the measured effect size will shrink.
 
\begin_inset Argument item:2
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

3-
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Separator plain
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Frame
