status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Why Contamination Matters?
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Bias in Results:

\series default
 Contamination typically leads to an underestimation of treatment effects,
 as both groups begin to resemble each other.
\begin_inset Argument 1
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

1-
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Reduced Validity:
 
\series default
The internal validity of the trial is compromised,
 making conclusions less reliable.
 
\begin_inset Argument item:2
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

2-
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Policy Implications:

\series default
 Contaminated trials can mislead healthcare guidelines,
 especially if the intervention appears less effective than it truly is.
 
\begin_inset Argument item:2
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

3-
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

